    "title": "This Old-School Missouri Coney Island Has Been Serving Chili Dogs Since 1983 - and Saturdays Still Pack the House - NewsBreak",
    "text": "5 hours ago Some restaurants chase trends every year. Others pick a lane in 1983 and simply stay in it. In Joplin, Missouri, one small spot has been turning out chili dogs, hand-pattied burgers, and fresh-cut fries for more than four decades, and the tables still fill up fast on Saturday afternoons. The menu is short on fuss and long on comfort food, with a few regional surprises that out-of-towners rarely expect. Read full article",
